  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 is the clearly best RNA encoder (0.5203 acc vs 0.4849 for pca_n2000 and 0.4106 for scgpt), and image-only is very weak (0.2079), suggesting RNA is the dominant signal. Uncertainty: we have only tested singleprofile so far and do not know whether multiprofile with aggregation improves the best RNA encoder. This experiment (config_005: rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) directly tests whether multiprofile + simple aggregation helps over the singleprofile baseline (config_004), changing only the profile/aggregation dimension while keeping the best encoder fixed. It is the best use of the next budget slot because it isolates the profile-setting effect on the strongest model, avoids confounding with image or fusion choices, and establishes whether the added complexity of multiprofile is worthwhile before investing in multimodal or transformer-aggregation variants."
}

